// D1541 — a value read out of a litunion ARRAY and delivered through an INLINE literal-union
// spelling. A litunion array is always the interned-i32 ATOM list, while a scalar litunion
// destination's rep follows the SPELLING (alias = atom, inline member set = string ref), so
// the two ends disagreed: the module-global cell was slotted as the atom and the READ took
// the plain-i32 arm, printing the interned id.
//
// NO `type` DECLARATION MAY BE ADDED. An alias whose member set is exactly the inline
// spelling's makes the annotation resolve to the alias's own arena index and both ends agree
// again — every cell then greens for the wrong reason. The value's source must stay a LIST
// ELEMENT: `const v: "red" | "green" = "green"` always ran.
//
// The PROOF prints the value, which is what discriminates the atom id from the member string.
//
// Format: scripts/capability-probes/matrix.py, whose docstring is the spec.
// @@PRELUDE@@
const srcArr: ("red" | "green")[] = ["green", "red"]
// @@VALUE@@
srcArr[0]
// @@TYPE@@
"red" | "green"
// @@PROOF@@
print(v)
// @@WANT@@
green
// @@VALUE2@@
srcArr[1]
// @@TYPE2@@
"red" | "green"
// @@PROOF2@@
print("c=" + v)
// @@WANT2@@
c=red
